# horizontalna mobilnost in the skill

**plan** The skill knew the ISVU catalog cold and knew nothing about the rules, so when someone asked the actual question ("studiram na FER-u, mogu li slušati predmete na PMF-u") it hedged. The old instructions literally said the rules "live on faculty websites, confirm with both student offices", which reads to a student as maybe they won't let you. I wanted it to answer the way I would: yes, this is a right, here is what actually varies.

Ran the same six probe questions past haiku, sonnet and opus as subagents, each fed the server instructions verbatim, before and after. Before, the three models failed in three different ways and only one of them was the failure I expected. Haiku affirmed on the two direct questions and then deflected all four substance ones with "to nije dostupno u katalogu", so 2/6. Sonnet affirmed 6/6 but invented the content: said mobility "uobičajeno se ne naplaćuje dodatno" (PMF charged me 7 eura for the molba) and said the grade goes into the matični studij like any other course, which gets the single most useful fact backwards since recognition is opt-in and failing costs nothing. Opus affirmed 6/6 and was the only one that refused to make numbers up ("ne mogu ti reći ni traženi prosjek ni cijenu bez izmišljanja"), but it passed on the FKIT link straight from the instructions and that URL 404s, the working page is a subpage under `/horizontalna_mobilnost/`.

The lesson is that giving it permission to say yes is not enough on its own. Sonnet already said yes and still misinformed the student, so the fix has to ship the actual rules or you just trade hedging for confabulation. So I wrote the rules down from the Smjernice za horizontalnu mobilnost (Odbor za upravljanje kvalitetom, 19.11.2024, KLASA 602-03/24-29/12) plus Pravilnik čl. 32, plus my own FER to PMF process from the video script, and marked clearly which bits are university wide and which are per faculty. Best line I found for the framing is FOI's own procedure, which opens with "studentu se odobrava ostvarenje **prava** na horizontalnu mobilnost". It is a right, in their words, not something anyone grants case by case. Useful detail from the Smjernice I did not know: for mobility the **razina** governs, not vrsta studija, so sveučilišni and stručni are interchangeable within a level (ZVOZD čl. 67(3), HKO čl. 7(6)). Also that the University audited every sastavnica's website in 2024 and found capacity limits "gotovo uopće nije dostupna online", which is the sentence that justifies telling a student that a missing page says something about that faculty's website and not about their rights.

Shipped it as a seventh MCP tool, `unizg_mobility_rules`, which makes no network call and just returns the briefing with sources and five verified links. The tool exists rather than only instruction text because the remote server on Vercel cannot read the repo, so the reference file is unreachable from the claude.ai app. The decisive core is inline in `INSTRUCTIONS` too, since the eval showed models answer these questions without calling anything. After the change all three models went 6/6 affirming, all three called the tool at P1 unprompted, and none invented a fee, a deadline or a prosjek threshold. Haiku 2/6 to 6/6 is the real win. Files: `api/_core.py` (`MOBILITY_RULES` + `INSTRUCTIONS`), `skills/unizg-courses/references/horizontalna-mobilnost.md` for the long version, `SKILL.md` description now triggers on dva fakulteta, drugi faks, paralelni studij, referada, molba.

Then I read haiku's actual Croatian instead of just counting verdicts, and found a second problem the score hid. All six answers were right on substance, but the Croatian was bad: "okončana prava" (concluded rights) where it meant an established right, "zavisi" instead of "ovisi", diacritics dropped off half the verbs, case errors, and the Cyrillic fragment "академ" sitting inside "rizika za академски prosječni uspjeh". Sonnet and opus wrote clean Croatian. My guess was that MOBILITY_RULES is written in ASCII folded Croatian (mogucnost, polozenih) so a small model copying terms had no correct spelling to anchor on, so I added a glossary of the right forms with diacritics. It fixed exactly the three defects I named in it and nothing else. Still there: studiras, polozis, trebas, pojavit ces without diacritics, "najprijed", "gebir" for a fee, "neke fakultete naplate", and "ne utječe na tvoj dom" which is a calque of home faculty that in Croatian says house. That is fluency, not instructions, and no amount of prompt text is going to fix it. So for the video and anything student facing in Croatian, haiku is fine for getting the facts right and not for writing the answer.

One small design thing worth remembering: `check_args` is deliberately strict and rejects unknown arguments, but a tool with no parameters now drops extras instead. A model asking for mobility rules "for FER" passes a stray `faculty`, and since the reply is identical whatever it gets there is no filter to silently drop, so the strictness protects nothing and a hard error just risks it abandoning a call it should make.

**todo** Deployed, both commits are on main and production serves the new tool with the glossary, checked live. The rok is the one fact I could not pin: my script has it as roughly a week from the start of nastava with a [__ provjeriti] on it, FOI says only "prije upisa u semestar u kojem ostvaruje mobilnost", and the central page gives no dates, so the reference says unverified and tells the student to ask. Would be worth checking what the actual deadline is at three or four faculties and putting real dates in. Also the eval only tested the rules half, never checked that a model combines it with a real catalog search in one answer (find Genetika across all 37, then explain the enrolment), which is the thing a student would actually ask for.

Sources: [Smjernice za horizontalnu mobilnost](https://www.unizg.hr/fileadmin/rektorat/Studiji_studiranje/Studiji/Kvaliteta/Kvaliteta1/Smjernice_za_horizontalnu_mobilnost_za_web.pdf) · [UNIZG central page](https://www.unizg.hr/studiji-i-studiranje/upisi-stipendije-priznavanja/horizontalna-mobilnost/) · [FOI procedura](https://www.foi.unizg.hr/hr/horizontalna-mobilnost) · my own process from `rector_award/video_yt/skripta.md`
